@@ -0,0 +1,400 @@
+---
+name: adr
+position: both
+description: 'Record a decision as an ADR, written from the one ADR template (standards/templates/adr.md) — a Markdown ADR for Garura''s own decisions (docs/adr/) or a decision.yaml record for a product decision — with what it overrides and what it changes in plain view: every older ADR it supersedes or amends (with the part), the files, rules, schemas, plays and agents it affects, its effect on agent intent (ICE), and whether it would change a person''s business intent (it never does: such a decision is shown to the person and not applied). Accepted only on a person''s word: run by hand, a pinned approval before anything is written as accepted; inside a drive, saved as proposed and accepted at the drive''s final review. Older ADRs gain only a forward pointer, written after acceptance; the ADR index is rebuilt. Also completes a proposed ADR later (/adr accept <file>). Run by hand it opens and lands its own change; handed a drive''s JSON contract it opens nothing of its own.'
+user-invocable: true
+---
+
+# adr
+
+Record a decision as an **ADR** — a decision record — from the one template in core memory,
+`standards/templates/adr.md`. One set of core fields, two shapes:
+
+- **Markdown** — Garura's own ADRs, `docs/adr/NNN-<slug>.md`.
+- **YAML** — a product decision, a `decision.yaml` (v2) record beside its node.
+
+The play makes what a decision overrides and what it changes visible before anyone accepts it,
+keeps every older ADR pointing forward, and never lets a decision change a person's business
+intent. Only a person accepts an ADR.
+
+**Pipeline position: both.** Run by hand, the D2 rule prepends `start-change` and appends
+`commit-change → propose-change → review-change → merge-change`. **Inside a drive** the drive
+hands it a JSON contract (`--contract`): it opens no issue or branch, skips the end sequence,
+does not stop for approval, and saves the ADR as proposed for the drive's final review
+(ADR 031).
+
+**Two entry modes.** `/adr <brief>` records a new decision. `/adr accept <file>` completes a
+proposed ADR later — the person accepts it, and its forward pointers and the index are written.
+
+## Compiled From
+
+This play was compiled from the adr ICE (`reference/ice.md`) by play-creator (#632). Intent
+defines constraints (C1–C11) and failure conditions (F1–F11); the expectation defines success
+scenarios (S1–S6), a Done means (D1–D5, baked to `stop-condition.yaml`), and one recovery entry
+per failure condition. To modify this play, update `reference/ice.md` and recompile with
+play-editor.
+Do NOT edit this file manually — it is a compiled artifact.
+
+## Role
+
+You are the orchestrator. You own the step order and the one human checkpoint. You hand the
+judgment — what the decision supersedes or amends, what it affects, its ICE impact, its
+business-intent check, and the draft — to the `adr-keeper` agent, which invokes the `author-adr`
+skill, through a JSON contract over files on disk. You run the mechanical work through bundled
+scripts: applying the person's word (`apply_adr.py`, over `adr.py`), the scope check and the
+stop condition. You never accept an ADR yourself, and you never edit an older ADR except
+through `apply_adr.py`'s forward pointer.
+
+**Forbidden:** writing a record without a complete brief (C1); writing off the template (C2);
+leaving an overridden ADR unnamed or without its part (C3); recording affects or ICE impact that
+names nothing real (C4); applying a decision that would change a person's business intent (C5);
+marking an ADR accepted without a person, writing a rejected one, or stopping for approval
+inside a drive (C6); editing an older ADR beyond its pointer, or pointing before acceptance
+(C7); leaving the index stale (C8); writing anything but the record, the pointers and the index
+(C9); opening an issue or branch inside a drive (C10); closing COMPLETED with the done checks
+unmet (C11).
+
+**Agent boundaries:**
+
+| Agent | Domain | Skill it invokes | Phases |
+|-------|--------|------------------|--------|
+| `adr-keeper` | Gather the context a decision needs (overlap candidates judged by reading them, affects, ICE impact, business-intent check), have the record drafted, check it (lint, guard) | `author-adr` | Draft |
+
+`adr-keeper` is the single **domain agent**. The start and end sequence are injected sub-plays.
+Everything else is a script.
+
+## Pre-flight
+
+| Check | Constraint | Action on Failure |
+|-------|-----------|-------------------|
+| Resolve config + `stm_base` (`.garura/core/config.yaml`) | — | Hard halt |
+| A decision brief was given: what is decided, why now, the options, who decides, where (or, for `accept`, a proposed ADR file) | C1 | Ask for what is missing (gather, not a halt) |
+| Drive contract: when `--contract <file>` is passed, it is valid JSON naming `drive_run_id` and `branch`, and the current branch equals that branch | C10 | Hard halt (REC10) |
+| The ADR template exists (`standards/templates/adr.md`) | C2 | Hard halt |
+
+Resolve the facts with the bundled resolver — not by inference:
+
+```
+git branch --show-current
+git status --porcelain -uall > <working>/porcelain-before.txt
+python3 scripts/preflight.py --play adr --config .garura/core/config.yaml \
+    --branch "<current branch>" --porcelain-file <working>/porcelain-before.txt
+python3 scripts/session_stamp.py --phase start \
+    --marker "{stm_base}{issue}/status/session-stamp-adr.json" \
+    --cwd "$(pwd)" --branch "$(git branch --show-current)"
+```
+
+`in_drive` is true exactly when a valid `--contract` was passed; record it in
+`<working>/run.json` with the contract's `drive_run_id` and `branch`. The working folder
+`<working>` is `{stm_base}{issue}/context/adr-<run-ts>/` (the drive's issue inside a drive).
+`porcelain-before.txt` is captured again after Step 0 when run by hand, so the scope check sees
+only this run's changes.
+
+## Task DAG
+
+Create ALL tasks immediately after pre-flight, before any domain work. Inside a drive, T0 and
+E1–E4 are created and marked skipped (`in_drive`), and T3 is skipped (no approval stop). In
+`accept` mode, T1 and T2 are skipped.
+
+```
+[T0] start-change (injected — start; skipped in a drive)   blockedBy: []
+[T1] Capture the brief                                    blockedBy: [T0]
+[T2] Draft the ADR (adr-keeper → author-adr)              blockedBy: [T1]
+[T3] Accept or reject (pinned by hand; none in a drive)   blockedBy: [T2]
+[T4] Apply: write, accept, point forward, index           blockedBy: [T3]
+[T5] Scope check                                          blockedBy: [T4]
+[T6] Commit the record                                    blockedBy: [T5]
+[E1] commit-change (injected — end; skipped in a drive)   blockedBy: [T6]
+[E2] propose-change (injected — end; skipped in a drive)  blockedBy: [E1]
+[E3] review-change (injected — end; skipped in a drive)   blockedBy: [E2]
+[E4] merge-change (injected — end; skipped in a drive)    blockedBy: [E3]
+[T7] Scenario Validation                                  blockedBy: [E4]
+[T8] Close                                                blockedBy: [T7]
+```
+
+Mark each task in progress before its step and completed right after its eval passes. No
+runtime reordering. On resume, skip completed and reset in-progress to pending.
+
+## Workflow
+
+### Phase: Start (injected — D2 position: start)
+
+**Step 0 — start-change** · Owner: `start-change` (sub-play) · Depends on: pre-flight
+*Skipped when `in_drive`.* Run the start-of-pipeline member as a sub-play with `parent_run_id`:
+it resolves or creates the issue, cuts the branch off fresh main, and inits STM. Then capture
+`git status --porcelain -uall > <working>/porcelain-before.txt` again on the new branch.
+
+    { "play": "start-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>",
+      "inputs": { "title": "adr: <the decision in a few words>" },
+      "outputs": { "result": "{stm_base}{issue}/context/adr-<run-ts>/start-change.json" } }
+
+### Phase: Brief
+
+**Step 1 — Capture the brief** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 0 · *skipped in `accept` mode*
+Write the decision brief to `<working>/brief.md` with these headings, in the person's (or the
+calling play's) words: `## Decision`, `## Why now`, `## Options considered` (each with why it
+lost), `## Decided by`, `## Decided in`, and the shape (`markdown` for a framework decision,
+`yaml` for a product decision, with its node). Ask the person for any heading that is empty —
+plainly, one at a time; never fill one in.
+**SE-1 (F1/C1):** `brief.md` has a non-empty Decision, Why now and Options considered; the
+agent's contract (Step 2) does not read `failed` with `brief_incomplete`.
+
+### Phase: Draft
+
+**Step 2 — Draft the ADR** · Owner: `adr-keeper` · Depends on: Step 1
+
+    { "task":    "gather the context for this decision and have it drafted as an ADR",
+      "inputs":  { "brief": "<working>/brief.md", "shape": "markdown | yaml",
+                   "adr_dir": "docs/adr (markdown) | <the node's decisions folder> (yaml)",
+                   "intents_dir": "<product_base>product-os/intents | null",
+                   "template_path": "<memory>/standards/templates/adr.md",
+                   "script": "<skill-dir>/scripts/adr.py" },
+      "outputs": { "context": "<working>/adr-context.yaml",
+                   "draft": "<working>/adr-draft.md | <working>/adr-draft.yaml",
+                   "check_report": "<working>/adr-check.json" },
+      "task_id": "draft-adr" }
+
+The agent finds the next number (or id), lists the overlap candidates and reads each to judge
+superseded / amended (with the part) / not affected, names what the decision affects and its
+ICE impact with real paths, sets the business-intent check (`none`, `kind` or `instance`), has
+`author-adr` draft the record as proposed, and checks it (lint and guard). It returns only its
+contract. `blocked` with `needs_person` means the decision would change a person's business
+intent, or the brief is incomplete — go to the person.
+**SE-2 (F2/C2):** `adr-check.json` reports the lint clean for the draft.
+**SE-3 (F3/C3):** `adr-context.yaml` lists every older ADR it supersedes or amends, each with a
+part; every ADR named in the draft's Supersedes/Amends is in that list and vice versa.
+**SE-4 (F4/C4):** the draft's Affects and ICE impact are non-empty, and every path in Affects
+exists in the repository.
+
+### Phase: Accept (pinned human checkpoint, run by hand)
+
+**Step 3 — Accept or reject** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 2 · Checkpoint (class:
+one-way-door, pinned) · **run by hand: never skipped by config or policy. Inside a drive:
+skipped — no approval stop.**
+*Inside a drive (`in_drive`), skip this step: the ADR is saved as proposed (Step 4 with
+`--proposed`), and the person accepts it at the drive's final review with `/adr accept <file>`.*
+If the business-intent check is `instance` (or the guard exits 4), stop here: show the person
+which business intent the decision would change and why, and close HALTED with
+`exit_reason: business_intent` — the person changes the brief or ends it (S2).
+Otherwise show the draft exactly as it will read, the older ADRs it supersedes or amends (with
+the part), what it affects, its ICE impact and its business-intent check, and ask the person to
+type one of: **accept**, **reject**, or **change: <what>**.
+- **accept** → write `<working>/decision.yaml`:
+  `decision: { verdict: accept, by: person, accepted_by: <git user>, reply: <their exact words> }`.
+- **reject** → write the same with `verdict: reject`; Step 4 writes nothing; close HALTED with
+  `exit_reason: rejected` (S5).
+- **change** → add the change to the brief and go back to Step 2.
+**SE-5 (F5/C5):** no record was applied while the business-intent check read `instance` or the
+guard exited 4.
+**SE-6 (F6/C6):** run by hand, `decision.yaml` reads `by: person` with the person's own
+non-empty reply, written only after the draft was shown; inside a drive, no `decision.yaml`
+exists and the play did not wait.
+
+### Phase: Apply
+
+**Step 4 — Apply: write, accept, point forward, index** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on:
+Step 3
+
+```
+python3 scripts/apply_adr.py --draft <working>/adr-draft.<md|yaml> \
+    --context <working>/adr-context.yaml --target <docs/adr/NNN-slug.md | <node>/decisions/<id>.yaml> \
+    ( --decision <working>/decision.yaml | --proposed ) \
+    --adr-dir <docs/adr | the node's decisions folder> [--index docs/adr/_index.md] \
+    [--intents-dir <product_base>product-os/intents] --date <date> --working <working>
+```
+
+In `accept` mode: `python3 scripts/apply_adr.py --accept-existing <file> --by "<git user>"
+--date <date> [--adr-dir docs/adr] [--index docs/adr/_index.md] --working <working>`, after the
+person typed **accept** on the proposed ADR shown to them.
+
+It lints, runs the business-intent guard (exit 4 stops before writing), writes nothing on a
+reject (exit 5), writes the record at the target (never over an existing file), and — only on
+accept — marks it accepted with the person's name, writes each forward pointer on the older
+ADRs (the only edit they get), and rebuilds the index. Inside a drive it saves the record as
+proposed and leaves the pointers for acceptance. It writes `adr-manifest.json`.
+**SE-7 (F7/C7):** every older ADR changed in this run differs from its base only on its Status
+line (Markdown) or its `superseded_by` / `amended_by` / `status` fields (YAML); no pointer was
+written while the record was proposed (`pointers_deferred: true`).
+**SE-8 (F8/C8):** for an accepted Markdown ADR, `adr-manifest.json` reads `index_ok: true`, and
+the index has a row for every ADR file in the folder.
+
+**Step 5 — Scope check** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on: Step 4
+
+```
+git status --porcelain -uall > <working>/porcelain-after.txt
+python3 scripts/check_adr_scope.py --before <working>/porcelain-before.txt \
+    --after <working>/porcelain-after.txt --allow <the target> \
+    --allow <each older ADR file it pointed> [--allow docs/adr/_index.md] \
+    --out <working>/guard-report.json
+```
+
+**SE-9 (F9/C9):** `guard-report.json` reads `ok: true` — only the record, its pointers, the
+index and the run's own records changed.
+
+**Step 6 — Commit the record** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 5
+
+```
+git add -- <the target> <each older ADR file it pointed> [docs/adr/_index.md] <working>
+git commit -m "docs(adr): ADR <NNN or id> — <title> (#<issue>)"
+```
+
+### Phase: End sequence (injected — D2 position: end)
+
+*Skipped when `in_drive` — the drive lands its own change.* After the commit, the D2 rule
+injects the close sequence, each a sub-play with `parent_run_id`:
+
+**Step E1 — commit-change** · blockedBy: Step 6
+
+    { "play": "commit-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "{stm_base}{issue}/context/adr-<run-ts>/commit-change.json" } }
+
+**Step E2 — propose-change** · blockedBy: E1
+
+    { "play": "propose-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "{stm_base}{issue}/context/adr-<run-ts>/propose-change.json" } }
+
+**Step E3 — review-change** · blockedBy: E2
+
+    { "play": "review-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "{stm_base}{issue}/context/adr-<run-ts>/review-change.json" } }
+
+**Step E4 — merge-change** · blockedBy: E3
+
+    { "play": "merge-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "{stm_base}{issue}/context/adr-<run-ts>/merge-change.json" } }
+
+Each end member owns its own evals; a review reject stops the chain before merge; the land on
+main keeps its pinned human approval.
+**SE-10 (F10/C10):** by hand, `start-change` ran at the head and `merge-change.json` reports the
+PR merged; inside a drive, `run.json` reads `in_drive: true`, neither `start-change` nor any end
+member ran, and the commit is on the contract's branch.
+
+### Phase: Scenario Validation
+
+**Step 7 — Scenario evals** · Owner: play · Depends on: the end sequence (or Step 6 in a drive)
+- **SCE-1 (S1 — framework author, amends older ADRs):** `adr-manifest.json` reads
+  `decided: true`, `status: accepted`, `lint_ok: true`, `linked: true`; each older ADR named in
+  the new one's Supersedes/Amends line carries a pointer to it on its Status line and is
+  otherwise unchanged.
+- **SCE-2 (S2 — framework author, would change a business intent):** the guard exited 4; no new
+  ADR file exists in the ADR folder; the run closed HALTED with `exit_reason: business_intent`.
+- **SCE-3 (S3 — product owner, product decision):** the record passes the lint, reads
+  `status: accepted` with `metadata.accepted_by`, and names its node.
+- **SCE-4 (S4 — Kickoff drive):** `run.json` reads `in_drive: true`; `adr-manifest.json` reads
+  `status: proposed` and `pointers_deferred: true`; no older ADR changed; no `decision.yaml`.
+- **SCE-5 (S5 — framework author, rejects):** `adr-manifest.json` reads `rejected: true`; no new
+  ADR file, no older ADR changed, the index unchanged; the run closed HALTED with
+  `exit_reason: rejected`.
+- **SCE-6 (S6 — framework author, the index):** the index has a row for the new number reading
+  Accepted, and a row for every ADR file in the folder.
+
+### Phase: Evidence & Close
+
+**Step 8 — Close** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 7
+Run the Standard Play Close.
+**SE-11 (F11/C11):** the close is stop-condition gated — `check_stop_condition.py` over the
+baked `stop-condition.yaml` (D1 record saved; D2 decided — accepted by a person, or proposed in
+a drive; D3 lint clean; D4 linked or pointers deferred; D5 scope ok) reads **held** before any
+COMPLETED close.
+
+```bash
+# --- Standard Play Close (canonical; see standards/rules/play-close.md) ---
+# Path tokens resolved at pre-flight (resolve here if not already):
+#   ltm_project_target  = yq '.ltm.project-target' .garura/core/config.yaml
+#   evidence_base, slug (project-scoped play):
+#     evidence_base="${stm_base}${issue}/evidence/adr/"   ; slug="#${issue}"
+evidence_template=$(cat "${ltm_project_target}standards/templates/evidence-file.md")
+delivery_template=$(cat "${ltm_project_target}standards/templates/delivery-report.md")
+ts=$(date -u +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
+evidence_dest="${evidence_base}${ts}.md"
+mkdir -p "$(dirname "$evidence_dest")"
+# Session identity stamp (#463) — close phase; start phase ran at pre-flight
+session_stamp=$(python3 scripts/session_stamp.py --phase close \
+    --marker "${stm_base}${issue}/status/session-stamp-adr.json")
+# Stop-condition gate (#464) — Step C0: this play carries a baked manifest, so the
+# gate is LIVE. Evaluate the Done means here as the close's authoritative input.
+python3 scripts/check_stop_condition.py \
+    --manifest "<play-dir>/stop-condition.yaml" \
+    --base "<working>/" \
+    --out "${stm_base}${issue}/status/stop-condition-adr.yaml"
+sc_exit=$?   # 0 held · 1 unmet · 2 error
+```
+
+**Step C0 — bind the verdict.** `sc_exit == 0` (held) permits `status: COMPLETED`. Anything
+else closes `HALTED` with `exit_reason: stop_condition_unmet` and the evidence's Stop Condition
+section names every unmet clause. A run the guard stopped closes HALTED with
+`exit_reason: business_intent`; a run the person rejected closes HALTED with
+`exit_reason: rejected`. An unevaluable verdict is never a pass.
+
+**Step C1 — Write evidence file.** Gated by the resolved `evidence.record` flag (global +
+per-play `evidence.plays.adr`; first match wins, absent ⇒ record). When false, skip the write
+and record `evidence skipped (record=false)` in the report's pointer line. Otherwise fill the
+`evidence-file.md` slots (play `adr`, run_id `adr-${ts}`, issue, started_at/completed_at,
+status per C0, exit_reason; artifacts produced: the record, the older ADRs pointed,
+the index, `brief.md`, `adr-context.yaml`, `adr-check.json`, `decision.yaml`,
+`adr-manifest.json`, `guard-report.json`, the commit sha; `in_drive`; step and scenario eval
+results SE-1…SE-11 / SCE-1…SCE-6; the checkpoint decision from Step 3 with the person's exact
+reply; the session identity stamp fields from $session_stamp (#463): session_id, ledger_file,
+ledger_start_offset, ledger_end_offset (null when unresolved — never blocks the close); and
+stop_condition per C0) and write to `$evidence_dest`. Do NOT hand-author the body.
+
+**Step C2 — Render delivery report.** Also render the **Next** line: resolve this play in
+`standards/rules/pipeline-next.md` and emit `**Next:** /<command> — <why>. Or run /next to see
+all recommended actions.` (only /next pointer, or omit, when the mapped command is null), per
+`play-close.md`. Fill the `delivery-report.md` slots and output the report:
+`## adr Delivered — ADR <NNN or id>`, the Run Summary table, the Pipeline Steps table from the
+task DAG, the Artifacts Produced table (the record, the pointers, the index), Next Steps (for a
+proposed ADR: accept it at the drive's final review with `/adr accept <file>`), and a pointer
+to `$evidence_dest`. Always emitted; never gated.
+
+```bash
+# --- end Standard Play Close ---
+```
